    "gap_definition": "Producer-accepted analysis of the 161-point W-L-Lambda-Gamma-Delta-X-Z-W-K path: G0W0 Gamma-point direct gap (valence-triplet top band 11 at 8.89423 eV, conduction band 14 at 10.81576 eV, both path edges at Gamma); diagonal-EXX minimum local gap 8.57826 eV at path point 64 on the Gamma-Delta segment with the Gamma-point local EXX gap 9.76976 eV; PBE path gap 0.73254 eV with edges at Gamma.",
    "notes": "df HPC path-only continuation of the validated SG15 8x8x8 source-mesh workflow (ABACUS band NSCF job 2487981 then LibRPA g0w0_band job 2487982, full-Coulomb EXX, nfreq 16, 66 bands with ABFS_ORBITAL pca1e-6) on the zincblende 2-atom primitive cell, spin-unpolarized; exported band tables carry uniform 2/161 k-weighted occupations for the 13 occupied bands (Z_val 20+6 over two spins). The scheduler marked the GW job FAILED on a post-run NaN gate, while LibRPA itself printed 'libRPA finished successfully' and the GW table is finite for bands 1-18; 33 higher-band NaN entries are retained and excluded from band-edge claims. A k12 mesh check differs by about 48.4 meV, so the gap is inside a small grid-change window but not all-numerical-parameter converged. Replaces the earlier 121-point KS HPC backup run per owner directive.",
    "gates": [],
    "scope": "Specific 3D geometry, SG15 v1.0 PP/NAO/ABF, k8 source mesh, 161-point path and numerical settings. All-band, empty-state, transferability and current-version acceptance not established by this audit."
